# TAP groups exercised by CI-tier-sweep (the merge-only v3.0/v3.1 sweep).
#
# Selection rule (enforced by test/infra/control/check_tier_sweep_groups.py):
#   a group is listed IFF
#     (1) it is already wired into regular CI -- a CI-<group>.yml caller, or
#         the name appears in a workflow on this branch or on origin/GH-Actions
#         (same "wired" definition as test/tap/groups/lint_group_coverage.py), AND
#     (2) at least one of its tests survives @proxysql_min_version on v3.0 OR
#         v3.1, i.e. the sweep can actually run something for it on some tier.
#
# Condition (1) is what keeps this honest: the sweep re-runs tests that regular
# CI already exercises on the v4.0 tier. Groups that no workflow ever selects are
# deliberately OUT of scope -- enabling them would conflate "does this tier
# work" with "does this group work at all", and 41 groups are in that state.
#
# A listed group whose tests are ALL gated out on the running tier is not an
# error: run-tests-isolated.bash skips it cleanly. ai-g2 is the current example
# -- it runs on v3.1 (1 test) and skips on v3.0 (0 tests).
#
# Do not hand-maintain group membership beyond adding/removing names; the lint
# check fails if this file and groups.json disagree in either direction.
#
#
ai-g1
ai-g2
